  "term": "pruning",
  "definition": "Pruning is the selective removal of parts of a model, such as channels or parameters, to make it smaller and more efficient while trying to preserve accuracy. In this source, adaptive pruning adjusts how much is removed based on feedback so communication and computation demands are reduced.",
